{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>To meet the serpents.</b> He ceased to calculate a propitious hour for curses to befall them, because he saw that it was good in the eyes of HaShem to bless them, and there was no reason to hope that he himself could curse them." "<b>And he set his face toward the wilderness.</b> To bless them with blessings mixed with harm among them, as the Sages of blessed memory said (Ta'anit 20): יָפָה קְלָלָה שֶׁקִּלֵּל אֲחִיָּה הַשִּׁלוֹנִי אֶת יִשְׂרָאֵל מִבְּרָכָה שֶׁבֵּרְכָם בִּלְעָם — \"Better was the curse that Ahijah the Shilonite cursed Israel than the blessing that Balaam blessed them.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:00.990911412Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}